\ ***************************************************************************
\ Writing the sound chip, through the System VIA's slow bus (after
\ chuckie-egg-2-beeb's sound.6502). The game includes it, and so does the
\ title page's music player in RSLOAD (rsload.6502), with the OS running:
\ it leaves the port as the OS's own writes do, with the keyboard back on
\ auto-scan, and holds interrupts off for each byte, so neither the OS's
\ keyboard interrupt nor the game's music interrupt can land inside one.
\ ***************************************************************************

\ Write A to the sound chip. X and Y are kept. (Y is kept with interrupts
\ off too: the game's interrupt calls this, and would overwrite sw_y.)
.sound_write
{
    PHP : SEI
    STY sw_y
    \ The keyboard off the bus first: key_down leaves it enabled, and then
    \ it drives port A's bit 7 (the addressed key's state), which would
    \ replace the byte's top bit.
    LDY #&0B : STY sysvia_orb
    LDY #&FF : STY sysvia_ddra
    STA sysvia_ora_nh
    LDY #0 : STY sysvia_orb         ; write enable low
    LDY #3                          ; ... for 8us
.hold
    DEY : BNE hold
    LDY #8 : STY sysvia_orb
    LDY sw_y
    PLP
    RTS
.sw_y EQUB 0
}
